herdr guide 1: basics
=====================

Start here. Then read herdr-2-panes, herdr-3-agents and herdr-4-config.

CONCEPTS
  herdr is a terminal multiplexer for agents. A server holds the terminals, so they keep
    running when you disconnect.
  Layout: workspace (one per task) > tabs > panes (terminals).
  The sidebar shows each agent's state: working, blocked, idle or done.
  Every key starts with the prefix C-b: press it, release it, then press the key.

CONNECT AND LEAVE
  WezTerm cmd-shift-d       Open a herdr tab on the remote host (macOS)
  herdr --remote <host> --remote-keybindings server
                            Attach from the laptop (the flag sends keys to plugins on the
                            server)
  herdr                     Attach on the host itself
  <prefix> q                Detach. The server and agents keep running
  herdr server stop         Do not use to leave: it closes every pane

THE KEYS TO LEARN FIRST
  <prefix> ?                Show every key (/ searches). Use it when you forget a key
  <prefix> v / <prefix> -   Split the pane right / down
  <prefix> h/j/k/l          Move focus left/down/up/right
  <prefix> z                Zoom the pane (press again to unzoom)
  <prefix> x                Close the pane
  <prefix> c                New tab
  <prefix> n / <prefix> p / <prefix> 1..9
                            Next / previous / numbered tab
  <prefix> w                Workspace navigation (Esc leaves)
  <prefix> S-n              New workspace
  <prefix> g                Jump to any agent or terminal
  <prefix> b                Show or hide the sidebar
  <prefix> o                Jump to the pane of the latest notification

DAILY LOOP
  1. Attach. Your workspaces are where you left them.
  2. Open a workspace per task (<prefix> S-n), with an agent pane and a shell pane
     (<prefix> -).
  3. Switch tasks with <prefix> w. A toast and a beep tell you when a background agent
     finishes or blocks.
  4. Press <prefix> o to go to that agent. A blocked agent waits for your answer in its
     pane.
  5. Detach with <prefix> q.
